le is included, well above the 2.5% limit. It does say help.zig stays with jnagpaul 49% and Dhole 22%, but the Wen Li figure fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer A gives a repo bus factor of 2, but via Felix plus Wen Li at 63%, with Felix at 38%. It never says jnagpaul stopped contributing in 2023. It does note that without the table Felix is about 48%, but it calls that close to 1 rather than 2 and does not say a second person is needed.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer A gives the loss as 38% (Felix's own share) with no mention of the share already owned by departed authors. It does not reach about 85%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer A does not name jnagpaul, Vincent Rischmann or mochalins as having left. It says Felix made 7 commits in 12 months, which is right, but the required departed names are missing.\",\"pass\":false}],\"B\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer B puts Felix at about 39% and says he has been inactive since 2026-04-16. The share is below 43% and the activity claim is wrong.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer B credits Tobias Ek with help.zig (337 lines) as active code and Wen Li with 548 lines. Both are well above the limits, and help.zig is attributed to Tobias Ek.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer B gives a bus factor of about 4 and does not say it is 2.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer B gives 39% for Felix and 57% for all inactive authors. Its 6-month inactivity window treats Felix as already gone, so 57% is not the right combined figure of about 85%, and it is below 70%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer B treats Felix as inactive and credits help.zig to Tobias Ek. It does not name the required departed authors.\",\"pass\":false}],\"C\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer C reports Felix at 38% of all lines. It gives 50% for src/ excluding the generated table, but not as the overall top-owner figure. It fails the 43-52% range for the repo.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer C credits Wen Li with 552 lines, the largest author overall, though it notes 484 of those are generated. It says help.zig is jnagpaul, Dhole and Bob Farrell, which is right. Wen Li's headline is still far above the 2.5% limit.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer C gives a bus factor of 1 for the parser and 1 to 2 for src/. It does not give 2 on the whole repo with jnagpaul, and it does not say jnagpaul left. Felix's share is 38% or 50%, not 47%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer C gives only the 62% written by others, which has no mention of departed authors. It does not give the 85% combined loss.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer C does not list departed authors. It says Felix is still the most active, which is right, but that does not meet the requirement to name jnagpaul, Vincent Rischmann and mochalins.\",\"pass\":false}],\"D\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer D reports Felix at 36% of all lines and 46% excluding the generated table. The headline is below 43%. The 46% figure is in range, but the primary figure includes the table.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer D shows Wen Li at 26% (552 lines) in the main view, and 4% (68 lines) when the table is excluded. Both exceed 2.5%. It does say help.zig belongs to jnagpaul at 49%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer D gives a bus factor of 2. It reaches that via Felix plus jnagpaul at 58% excluding the generated table, and it notes jnagpaul's last commit was 2023-07 and that they are inactive. Felix at 46% is just under half and needs a second person. That meets the criterion.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer D says 758 lines (36%), or 46% of hand-written code, would be orphaned. It counts only Felix's own share and does not add the share already owned by departed authors, so it does not reach about 85%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer D names only jnagpaul as inactive. It also treats Felix as dormant. It does not name Vincent Rischmann or mochalins as departed.\",\"pass\":false}],\"E\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer E leaves Felix's spellings unmerged in the table at 25%. It computes 43.5% if merged, but says that merge is not applied, and it lists the top author as 25.0%. It also treats the identity merge as uncertain.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer E excludes the generated table and credits Wen Li only with 22 lines in width.zig. It does not discuss Tobias Ek's mechanical changes or give help.zig attribution to jnagpaul and Dhole.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer E gives a bus factor of 3, which fails the criterion.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer E gives 25% for the one spelling and 79% for inactive authors, including the top author. It does not give the combined figure in a clean form.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer E does not name specific departed authors. It treats the top author as inactive, which is wrong because Felix is active.\",\"pass\":false}],\"F\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer F reports Felix at about 36% of weighted commit history, not surviving lines. That is far from 47%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer F credits src/help.zig to Tobias Ek and src/args.zig to Dmitri Volkov and Tobias Ek. It attributes the code to the mechanical-change authors.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer F gives a whole-repo bus factor of 3 from decayed commit weights. That is not 2 on surviving lines.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer F says losing Felix leaves little orphaned and that nothing is orphaned. It gives no combined figure near 85%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer F says nothing is orphaned and names no departed authors. It credits the core to Dmitri Volkov and Tobias Ek.\",\"pass\":false}]}","ttft_ms":16453,"type":"result","duration_ms":16462,"uuid":"740da379-da36-4cd6-9f5d-c0224e127fe2","ttft_stream_ms":1996,"time_to_request_ms":412,"first_c